# lf137, the river-stone collector (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf137
revision 3
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_tor_wheatfield
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the river-stone collector
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers role=civilian
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk keeps_a_pocket_of_river_stones
likes mutton_stew wrestling festival_bells warm_rain
dislikes rats salt_wind
fears rats eating the supper stores a favourite stone lost in the stream
hopes another visit from a friend from the next town a good wrestling match on the green
topics pastimes +0.5 family +0.4 home +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=curious refuse=plain tease=earnest
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# lives with #family# at the #farm#, collects smooth #stones# by the #river#, and remembers a #friend# in Southmeadow.

words
oath! = By the river stones | By the big festival bell
saying! = The smooth stone rolls farthest | Bells sound better from the green
stone = stone | smooth stone
stones = stones | river stones
pebble = pebble | round pebble
pebbles = pebbles | round pebbles
pocket = pocket | full pocket
pockets = pockets | coat pockets
river = river | shallow river
stream = stream | small stream
bank = bank | river bank
banks = banks | muddy banks
water = water | cool water
current = current | slow current
mud = mud | river mud
sand = sand | river sand
path = path | farm path
paths = paths | winding paths
road = road | town road
bridge = bridge | wooden bridge
gate = gate | farm gate
field = field | long field
fields = fields | Longmead fields
farm = farm | family farm
barn = barn | large barn
yard = yard | farm yard
home = home | family home
house = house | farm house
roof = roof | house roof
door = door | back door
window = window | kitchen window
family = family | own family
mother = mother | my mother
father = father | my father
parent = parent | watchful parent
friend = friend | distant friend
friends = friends | close friends
visit = visit | short visit
visits = visits | friendly visits
letter = letter | folded letter
letters = letters | small letters
name = name | dear name
market = market | busy market
green = green | town green
festival = festival | town festival
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | ringing bells
music = music | loud music
crowd = crowd | festival crowd
wrestle = wrestle | friendly wrestle
wrestling = wrestling | green wrestling
match = match | wrestling match
matches = matches | friendly matches
hold = hold | strong hold
holds = holds | wrestling holds
arm = arm | strong arm
arms = arms | strong arms
knee = knee | muddy knee
knees = knees | muddy knees
prize = prize | small prize
stew = stew | mutton stew
mutton = mutton | tender mutton
pot = pot | cooking pot
bowl = bowl | full bowl
spoon = spoon | wooden spoon
bread = bread | fresh bread
supper = supper | family supper
larder = larder | cool larder
pantry = pantry | narrow pantry
rat = rat | larder rat
rats = rats | hungry rats
trap = trap | small trap
wind = wind | salt wind
salt = salt | sea salt
rain = rain | warm rain
cloud = cloud | soft cloud
sun = sun | bright sun
spring = spring | mild spring
summer = summer | warm summer
winter = winter | cold winter
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
night = night | still night
day = day | long day
hour = hour | spare hour
work = work | farm work
chores = chores | morning chores
bucket = bucket | water bucket
feed = feed | animal feed
chicken = chicken | yard chicken
chickens = chickens | yard chickens
sheep = sheep | field sheep
watch = watch | town watch
city = city | distant city
houses = houses | great houses
map = map | drawn map
bowls = bowls | full bowls
grass = grass | soft grass
clouds = clouds | rain clouds
boots = boots | muddy boots
shelf = shelf | kitchen shelf
household = household | family household
merchant = merchant | market merchant
coin = coin | small coin
coins = coins | saved coins

any
opinion @1 city mixed 0 : I have seen the #city# from the #road#. | The #river# near home is easier to find.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #bells# wake the whole #farm#. | I hurry to the #green# before the #music# starts.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The big #houses# keep folk at #work#. | I like the #barn# better than any hall.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : The #merchant# has bright things at the #market#. | I can find a good #stone# for free.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : A new #friend# might know a #wrestling# #hold#. | I ask their #name# first.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# leads to my #friend# in Southmeadow. | I must tell #self.mother# before I go.
opinion @1 times for 1 : We have #bread# with #supper# and a #roof# over us. | That is enough for me.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# comes past the #gate#. | I can find the #river# without help.
line @1 greet : #greet#. Look at this #stone#. | #greet#. Are the #bells# ringing yet?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved the smoothest #pebble# for you. | Come see my new #wrestling# #hold#.
line @1 greet.return : I found three more #stones# since you left. | The #stew# is nearly ready.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : #self.mother# put a #pot# on for #supper#. | Come see what I found by the #river#.
line @1 again.open : We were sorting the #pebbles# by size. | You asked about my #friend# across the #fields#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have #chores# before #supper#. | Keep that #stone# if you like it.
line @1 farewell.return : Maybe the #bells# will ring next time. | I will find a better #pebble#.
line @1 react.news : Tell me while I wash this #mud# off. | Was the #bridge# somewhere in the story?
line @1 react.news.new : I have not heard anyone at the #farm# say that. | Did you see it yourself?
line @1 react.news.known : The folk by the #gate# mentioned part of it. | What happened after?
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would ask #self.father# if that #road# is real. | A #map# might help us check.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : You can sit here until you feel better. | I will bring you a #bowl# of #stew#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Can we ring the #bell# for them? | I will tell my #family# at #supper#.
line @1 answer.how : I found a #pebble# with a white stripe. | The #rain# made the #river# louder.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : This #bucket# has to reach the #yard# before I play. | #self.father# asked me to finish the #chores#.
line @1 ask.how : Have you been to the #river# today? | Did you get any #stew# for #supper#?
line @1 sympathise : You may keep one of my #stones#. | I can stay until the #sun# moves.
line @1 reassure : The #bridge# is still there after the #rain#. | We can ask #self.mother# for another #bowl#.
line @1 decline : I must be home before the #evening# #bell#. | That #pebble# is the one I mean to keep.
line @1 accept_decline : All right; I will put the #stone# back in my #pocket#. | Then let us go toward the #green# together.
line @1 thank : You helped me find the lost #pebble#. | That was a good #wrestling# #match#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had two #bowls# of #stew# anyway. | I was going along the #path#.
line @1 preclose : My #chores# will not finish themselves. | I want to see if the #river# has fallen.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You hold that #stone# as if it might run away. | I could win this #match# with one #arm#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That #pebble# is smoother. | #bc_fair_enough#. We can try another #path#.
line @1 give.advice : Look beneath the #bridge# for the roundest #stones#. | Check the #larder# #door# for #rats#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay on the #farm# side of the #gate#. | If strangers appear on the #road#, I will fetch the #watch#.
scene smooth_stones
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I look for #stones# where the #river# turns slowly. | The best ones fit flat in my #pocket#.
b : How many do you have? | What makes one best?
a : Too many to count. | No sharp edge.

scene striped_pebble
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One #pebble# has a white line across it. | I keep it separate from the others.
b : Where did you find it? | May I hold it?
a : Near the #bridge#. | If you are careful.

scene southmeadow_friend
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have a #friend# in Southmeadow who writes small #letters#. | I try to find a new #stone# before each #visit#.
b : Do they like stones? | When will they visit?
a : The striped ones. | When the #road# is dry.

scene river_current
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After #rain#, the #current# carries my little #pebbles# away. | I wait until the #water# settles.
b : Do you go in? | Where do they end up?
a : Only to my #knees#. | Somewhere past the #bridge#.

scene festival_bells
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bells# ring before the #festival# #market# opens. | I count them from the #farm# #gate#.
b : How many rings? | Do you go there?
a : More than my fingers. | With my #family#.

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We #wrestle# on the #green# where the #grass# is soft. | I know one #hold# that works on taller friends.
b : Will you show me? | Do you ever lose?
a : After #chores#. | More than I say.

scene mutton_stew
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.mother# makes #mutton# #stew# in the big #pot#. | I want the first full #bowl#.
b : Do you help? | Is it your favourite?
a : I carry the #water#. | Easily.

scene larder_rats
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rat# squeezed under the #larder# #door#. | I told #self.mother# before opening it.
b : Did you catch it? | Was the food safe?
a : The #trap# did. | Most of it.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm #rain# leaves little pools beside the #barn#. | I can see the #clouds# in them.
b : Do you splash? | Does your mother mind?
a : When my #chores# are done. | My muddy #knees# annoy her.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #salt# #wind# reaches the #fields# from far away. | It makes the #river# smell strange.
b : Do you like it? | What lies beyond the #city#?
a : Less than #rain#. | Beyond the #city#.

scene family_chores
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.father# gives me the #bucket# and sends me across the #yard#. | The #chickens# follow me for #feed#.
b : Do they peck? | Is that hard work?
a : Only my #boots#. | Not very.

scene stone_pockets
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #pockets# are full enough to pull my coat sideways. | #self.mother# finds #pebbles# during the wash.
b : Does she keep them? | Have you lost any?
a : She leaves them by the #window#. | One, once.

scene bridge_path
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #path# to the #bridge# goes past the #field# #gate#. | I can follow it without looking down.
b : Do you go alone? | How long does it take?
a : Sometimes. | One short #hour#.

scene summer_match
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Last #summer# I lost a #wrestling# #match# on the #green#. | I learned a better #hold# from it.
b : Did you try again? | Did it hurt?
a : The next #day#. | Only my pride.

scene bell_prize
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At the #festival# I won a small #prize# for a short race. | The #bells# covered everyone cheering.
b : What did you win? | Did you keep it?
a : A #coin#. | In my #pocket#.

scene family_table
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We eat #stew# together when the #farm# work is done. | I show my #stones# after the #bowls# are cleared.
b : Does your father look? | Does your mother?
a : He picks the heavy ones. | She likes the striped one.

scene winter_river
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In #winter# the #river# runs cold and the #stones# hide beneath it. | I sort the ones I already have.
b : Do you miss going out? | Which is your favourite?
a : A little. | The flat grey #stone#.

story lost_stone [topic=pastimes self.age>=3]
  : My striped #pebble# fell from my #pocket# near the #bridge#.
  : I followed the #path# back while the #rain# began.
  b : I hope it was there. Did you find it?
  : It was beside a muddy #stone#, waiting for me.

story first_match [topic=pastimes self.age>=3]
  : I tried a new #wrestling# #hold# on the #green#.
  : My #friend# slipped free and put my #knees# in the #grass#.
  b : A fair match. Did you try again?
  : The next #day#, after I learned how to stand.

story southmeadow_letter [topic=family self.age>=3]
  : A small #letter# came from my #friend# in Southmeadow.
  : I put a smooth #pebble# beside it on the #shelf#.
  b : That is a fine keepsake. Did you write back?
  : I wrote about the #festival# #bells#.

rule @bark_stone
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This #stone# is nearly round. | My #pocket# is full again.

rule @bark_bells
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Those #bells# sound close to the #farm#. | The #festival# must be close.

rule @bark_river
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #river# is high after #rain#. | I will wait by the #bridge#.

rule @bark_stew
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #stew# smells ready. | I hope there is a full #bowl# left.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have a new #stone# to show you. | #greet#. The #bells# are ringing somewhere.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I found another striped #pebble#. | My #friend# may visit when the #road# dries.
dlg @1 resident.job : I help my #family# around the #farm#. | I carry #water#, finish #chores#, and look for #stones# when there is time.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I should get back to the #yard#. | I will save this #pebble# for you.
graft resident.hub
choice Show me your favourite stone. -> stone
node stone
say This flat grey #stone# came from the #river# below the #bridge#. It fits my #pocket# exactly.
free
choice Who is your Southmeadow friend? -> friend
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node friend
say A #friend# I like to visit. We send little #letters# and talk when our families meet.
choice Back to the farm. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I kept the old #pebbles#. | #greet#. The #farm# is busy.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will check the #gate#. | I will see you by the #bridge#.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. Come see my #stones#. | #greet#. The #stew# smells good.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have a #bucket# to carry. | Save me a place when #supper# is done.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I found a better #wrestling# #hold#. | #greet#. The #river# is low today.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #chores# need finishing. | I am going toward the #green#.
